 "about_text": "Mizoe Art Gallery was founded in Fukuoka in 2008 and opened a second space in Tokyo's Denenchofu neighborhood in 2012, linking the Kyushu and Tokyo art scenes and presenting Japanese art internationally. Both locations occupy detached houses set in large gardens in quiet residential areas; the Tokyo gallery is housed in a traditional Japanese-style residence where works are shown room by room. The gallery states its guiding concept as offering high-quality works and artists unaffected by trends or eras, favoring art of lasting, universal value. Its program spans modern and postwar Japanese painters and sculptors alongside major Western modern masters.",
